Description: operator-grade resource monitor (fork of GNOME System Monitor)
 A fork of GNOME System Monitor 50.0 that reports what each figure measures,
 groups load by who is responsible for it, and adds a Health tab with storage
 wear, per-process write blame and component lifespan.
 .
 The binary is gnome-system-monitor-rh; /usr/bin/gnome-system-monitor is a
 symlink to it. This package replaces the distribution's gnome-system-monitor.
 Privileged actions (signals, renice, affinity) go through root-owned
 helpers in /usr/libexec/gnome-system-monitor, run with pkexec. SMART data of
 USB-attached drives is read by a hardened, read-only system service
 (gsm-smart-reader.service) that a timer runs every 10 minutes and that
 needs no password; it is enabled on install and
 "systemctl disable --now gsm-smart-reader.timer" turns it off. NVMe and
 SATA drives are read through udisks2.
